{
  "class": "PlayerInfoUpdatePacket",
  "module": "server/play/player_info_update_packet",
  "module_docs": [
    "Port of",
    "`net.minestom.server.network.packet.server.play.PlayerInfoUpdatePacket`",
    "and its nested `Entry`, `Property` and `Action` declarations.",
    "",
    "# Deferrals",
    "",
    "- `crypto.ChatSession.SERIALIZER` writes a session UUID and a",
    "  `PlayerPublicKey` (an expiry instant, an X.509-encoded RSA public key and",
    "  a signature). The ported `crypto::ChatSession` carries only the UUID, so",
    "  [`ChatSessionRef`] declares the wire shape here. The public key is kept as",
    "  its opaque DER bytes \u2014 nothing in the packet path decodes it.",
    "- `components()` / `copyWithOperator` come from",
    "  `ServerPacket.ComponentHolding`, ported as `ComponentHoldingServerPacket`",
    "  (`super::super::server_packet`).",
    "",
    "Java's compact constructor copies both collections; `EnumSet.copyOf` keeps",
    "the constants in **declaration order**, so the port stores a `Vec<Action>`",
    "that the entry serializer walks in that order, and the `Action` bit set is",
    "written as Java's `EnumSet(Action.class)` (a one-byte fixed bit set, because",
    "`Action` has eight constants)."
  ],
